  "name": "wan-baseline",
  "description": "Constant 50ms ±10ms inter-container latency applied to all ring-50 services from t=1s, simulating a DC-to-DC WAN link as a permanent baseline condition. NOT one of the paper's original four fault profiles — this is future-work validation for the external validity concern raised in Section 2 (Threats to Validity). With 50ms RTT and gossip interval 3000ms, ring-50 convergence takes ~2.5s per hop vs ~5ms at zero baseline. Use alongside an active fault profile (e.g. baseline-flaky) to test whether strategy rankings hold under non-zero baseline latency.",
